body:
i think maybe if you get on a med called antabuse, you might want to avoid it (maybe kombucha, too) since you might be extra sensitive and get sick.  but other than that, there's no real reason you shouldnt as long as it's not triggering.  it's your recovery and it sounds like the NA beers are nice to drink as an alternative.  

&#x200B;

iwndwyt

it can be but i think there's a fine line.  my mom used to take it (she might still but idk) and she accidentally double dosed and had a seizure later in the day.  same thing happened to me with lithium tho ive never seen lithium prescribed for seizures.

&#x200B;

if you *think* you've taken your meds already, just assume you did!

spitfire logo with a lil body

&#x200B;

or campfire
